    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_8bb7c5afd9b4453747a2a26a1975ba2962d9b37e39b4050b2de577d1b5135564",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The span establishes two distinct kinds of admissibility for the later closure problem. B(g) records finite linear reach from g using only the positive-integer dilations K_n, even though K_lambda is available and bounded for every positive lambda; separately, Mellin analyticity on 0<Re(s)<1 is asserted only under membership in every Lp with 1<p<infinity. Thus the definitions supply compatible function-space, dilation-hull, and analytic vocabulary, but this span neither closes B(g) nor proves any transform law connecting dilation to the Mellin variable.",
