    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1e5a0f7ae260b671a8f464f35d0946210720f0b9cdb407d3c180b3aa05df5496",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The RH-conditioned closure witness for the classical pair is transported to any good kernel: T_{f'} commutes with dilations, maps rho_1 to P f and chi to -f, and is L2-bounded, so applying it to approximants in B(rho_1) preserves both generated-span membership and convergence to the new target. The generalized necessity result therefore reuses the classical approximation instead of constructing a new Gramian witness kernel by kernel.",
