    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_808dd31835037f4bfcbeece51d4eb48fba15c71d1faeb8a1c7c3483e2713d3b9",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source connects three representations of P by discharging the analytic obligations between them. The formal sum-integral discrepancy is first made meaningful almost everywhere by an absolute sampling bound; integration by parts, boundary decay, and Burnol convergence then identify it with T_{f'}rho_1 and yield Lp control; finally Mellin factorization, with a separate absolute-integrability calculation justifying Fubini, turns that pseudo-convolution into multiplication of f-hat by zeta.",
