    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ff8b180d007a7a3f4ab58276b7e850f81e9b52215b56144a8514168c45f7f8e6",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The paper changes the necessity-side proof geometry without claiming to solve the original distance problem. The classical route seeks explicit Gramian distances among rho_1 dilates, while the generalized route applies a bounded dilation-commuting operator to an existing RH-conditioned approximation and thereby preserves span membership and convergence for every good kernel. This transport widens the search to kernels chosen for potentially simpler scalar products, even though the resulting strong-kernel family is not known to be closed under addition.",
